{"questions":[{"question_id":"zwxICMBr9jWLHy1A","paperTitle":"JEE Advanced 2014 Paper 1 Offline","year":2014,"examDate":2014,"subject":"chemistry","chapter":"some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry","chapterGroup":"physical-chemistry","topic":"concentration-terms","type":"integer","marks":3,"negMarks":0,"permalink":"a-compound-h2x-with-molar-weight-of-80g-is-dissolved-in-a-so-2014-marks-3-zwxicmbr9jwlhy1a.htm","content":"A compound H<sub>2</sub>X with molar weight of 80g is dissolved in a solvent having density of 0.4 gml<sup>–1</sup> . Assuming no change in volume upon dissolution, the molality of a 3.2 molar solution is","options":[],"correct_options":[],"explanation":"<strong>Understanding the Concepts</strong>\n\n<br><br><li><strong>Molarity (M):</strong> Moles of solute per liter of solution.</li><br>\n\n<li><strong>Molality (m):</strong> Moles of solute per kilogram of solvent.</li><br>\n\n<li><strong>Density:</strong> Mass per unit volume.</li>\n\n<br><strong>Steps to Calculate Molality</strong>\n\n<ol>\n\n<br><li><strong>Find the Mass of Solute (H₂X):</strong></li>\n\n</ol>\n\n<ul>\n\n<br><li>Molarity = moles of solute / volume of solution (in liters)</li><br>\n\n<li>3.2 M solution means 3.2 moles of H₂X are present in 1 liter of solution.</li><br>\n\n<li>Mass of H₂X = moles <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0.02ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.09ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -491 778 482\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"D7\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-D7\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> molar mass = 3.2 moles <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0.02ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.09ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -491 778 482\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"D7\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-D7\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> 80 g/mole = 256 g</li>\n\n</ul>\n\n<ol>\n\n<br><li><strong>Find the Mass of Solvent:</strong></li>\n\n</ol>\n\n<ul>\n\n<br><li>Assuming no change in volume, the volume of the solution remains 1 liter.</li><br>\n\n<li>Density = mass / volume</li><br>\n\n<li>Mass of solvent = density <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0.02ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.09ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -491 778 482\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"D7\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-D7\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> volume = 0.4 g/mL <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0.02ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.09ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -491 778 482\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"D7\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-D7\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> 1000 mL = 400 g</li>\n\n</ul>\n\n<ol>\n\n<br><li><strong>Convert Mass of Solvent to Kilograms:</strong></li>\n\n</ol>\n\n<ul>\n\n<br><li>1 kg = 1000 g</li><br>\n\n<li>Mass of solvent = 400 g <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0.02ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.09ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -491 778 482\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"D7\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-D7\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> (1 kg / 1000 g) = 0.4 kg</li>\n\n</ul>\n\n<ol>\n\n<br><li><strong>Calculate Molality:</strong></li>\n\n</ol>\n\n<ul>\n\n<br><li>Molality = moles of solute / mass of solvent (in kg)</li><br>\n\n<li>Molality = 3.2 moles / 0.4 kg = 8 mol/kg</li>\n\n</ul>\n\n<br><strong>Answer:</strong>\n\n<p>The molality of the 3.2 molar solution is 8 mol/kg.</p>\n\n<p></p>"}]}